erformance 48% far below SOTA (GAGPO 93.5%, HiPER 97.4%).\n- Contribution is diagnostic/methodological, not performance-focused.\n- Selective verification tested on only two environments.\n\n## Your Review Task\n\nProvide a detailed review covering:\n\n1. **Novelty Assessment**:\n   - Is the dual mechanism diagnosis genuinely new? Turn-PPO already identified the \"uniform advantage\" problem. What is the incremental contribution?\n   - Is the \"episode-level info matters more than finer credit\" finding surprising or expected?\n   - Is B-IAVR (action-change reward for verification routing) a significant methodological contribution?\n   - How does this compare to Thinkless which also uses RL for binary control tokens?\n\n2. **Related Work Adequacy**:\n   - Are key competitors properly cited and discussed?\n   - Is the positioning honest given the huge performance gap (48% vs 93.5-97.4%)?\n   - Are there missing references?\n\n3. **Significance and Impact**:\n   - Who benefits from this work? Practitioners or researchers?\n   - Is the contrarian \"coarser is better\" finding likely to influence the field?\n   - Is the B-IAVR component likely to be adopted?\n\n4. **Claim Validity vs. Framing**:\n   - Does the paper overclaim? Are the contributions fairly stated?\n   - Is the \"finer credit is unnecessary\" claim too strong given the limited setting (sparse binary rewards)?\n   - The paper says GAGPO/HiPER use \"finer-grained credit assignment and larger models\" — is this a fair characterization?\n\n5. **Weaknesses**: Be specific. Classify as (major) or (minor).\n\n6. **Questions for authors**: 3-5 specific questions.\n\n7. **Preliminary Score**: X/6 with justification.\n\nFormat your review as a structured document with headers. Be thorough but fair."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01M8ccfgPjsRhMzeCytoYGzb","session_id":"865e8d8a-d167-43f7-87ae-b7ba5c42080f","uuid":"41763152-4fcd-4394-8667-35e07a9142d8","timestamp":"2026-05-17T14:01:13.162Z"}
