{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017ohZRcUg7r566aUkasL5jj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 竞品论文验证报告 (2026-05-17)\n2\t\n3\t## 1. GAGPO (2605.13217) — 验证通过\n4\t\n5\t- **arXiv ID**: 2605.13217 → 指向正确论文\n6\t- **标题**: \"GAGPO: Generalized Advantage Grouped Policy Optimization\"\n7\t  - 注意：任务描述中的 \"Grouped Value Proxy + Temporal Credit Propagation\" 不是论文标题组成部分，但 \"Grouped Value Proxy\" 是论文中核心机制的术语，\"recursively propagating outcome supervision backward through time\" 对应 Temporal Credit Propagation 概念\n8\t- **作者**: Siyuan Zhu, Chao Yu, Rongxin Yang, Zongkai Liu, Jinjun Hu, Qiwen Chen, Yibo Zhang\n9\t- **Venue/Year**: arXiv, May 2026\n10\t- **关键实验数据**:\n11\t  - ALFWorld 93.5±1.3% (Qwen2.5-1.5B) — 与声称一致\n12\t  - ALFWorld 95.6±0.9% (Qwen2.5-7B)\n13\t  - WebShop 88.6±3.3 score / 78.1% success (1.5B)\n14\t  - GRPO baseline: 70.3% (1.5B), 73.2% (7B)\n15\t  - GiGPO baseline: 88.1% (1.5B), 88.8% (7B)\n16\t- **方法**: 非参数 grouped value proxy + TD/GAE-style step advantages + group-normalized PPO update, critic-free\n17\t- **与我们的关系**: 追求更细粒度 credit assignment 以提高性能；我们诊断为什么 step-independent 失败\n18\t\n19\t## 2. MT-GRPO (2505.11821) — 验证通过（需修正描述）\n20\t\n21\t- **arXiv ID**: 2505.11821 → 指向正确论文\n22\t- **标题**: \"Reinforcing Multi-Turn Reasoning in LLM Agents via Turn-Level Reward Design\"\n23\t- **作者**: Quan Wei, Siliang Zeng, Chenliang Li, William Brown, Oana Frunza, Wei Deng, Anderson Schneider, Yuriy Nevmyvaka, Yang Katie Zhao, Alfredo Garcia, Mingyi Hong\n24\t- **Venue/Year**: arXiv, May 2025 (revised Oct 2025)\n25\t- **关键实验数据**:\n26\t  - 评测在 QA 数据集（NQ, TriviaQA, PopQA, HotpotQA, 2WikiMultiHopQA, Musique）\n27\t  - 不包含 ALFWorld\n28\t  - 使用 Qwen2.5-7B\n29\t  - MT-GRPO 术语在 Section 3.2 中正式使用\n30\t  - 近 100% format correctness, answer correctness ~0.45-0.65 across datasets\n31\t- **修正**: 该论文是 turn-level reward design for search/QA tasks，非 ALFWorld agent 任务\n32\t- **与我们的关系**: 同样发现 turn-level credit 优于 trajectory-level；我们的 contrarian 结论是 episode-level (coarser) 反而消除 sign misattribution\n33\t\n34\t## 3. iStar (2509.19199) — 验证通过\n35\t\n36\t- **arXiv ID**: 2509.19199 → 指向正确论文\n37\t- **标题**: \"Agentic Reinforcement Learning with Implicit Step Rewards\"\n38\t- **作者**: Xiaoqian Liu, Ke Wang, Yuchuan Wu, Fei Huang, Yongbin Li, Junge Zhang, Jianbin Jiao\n39\t- **Venue/Year**: ICLR 2026（OpenReview 确认: openreview.net/forum?id=ooROvpmxMV）\n40\t- **关键实验数据**:\n41\t  - WebShop: 86.5±2.8% success, 93.6±1.0 score (Qwen2.5-7B)\n42\t  - VisualSokoban: 91.7% success (Qwen2.5-VL-7B)\n43\t  - SOTOPIA: +48% goal completion vs GPT-4o (Llama3.1-8B)\n44\t  - 不包含 ALFWorld 评测\n45\t- **方法**: Implicit PRM (trajectory DPO objective) + dual advantage (step-level + episode-level)\n46\t- **与我们的关系**: 追求更细粒度 step-level credit (通过学习 implicit rewards)；我们展示 episode-level 单独即可消除 sign misattribution\n47\t\n48\t## 4. ArCHer (2402.19446) — 验证通过\n49\t\n50\t- **arXiv ID**: 2402.19446 → 指向正确论文\n51\t- **标题**: \"ArCHer: Training Language Model Agents via Hierarchical Multi-Turn RL\"\n52\t- **作者**: Yifei Zhou, Andrea Zanette, Jiayi Pan, Sergey Levine, Aviral Kumar\n53\t- **Venue/Year**: ICML 2024（icml.cc/virtual/2024/poster/33654 确认）\n54\t- **关键实验数据**:\n55\t  - ~100x sample efficiency improvement over flat RL\n56\t  - 验证至 7B 参数规模\n57\t  - 评测：web interaction, tool use, customer support\n58\t- **方法**: 高层 off-policy value-based RL（utterance 级 Q-function）+ 低层 token policy (within-turn)\n59\t- **与我们的关系**: 开创性框架，建立 multi-turn RL 需要层次结构的共识；我们具体诊断为什么 flat step-independent 失败\n60\t\n61\t## 5. CA Survey (2604.09459) — 验证通过\n62\t\n63\t- **arXiv ID**: 2604.09459 → 指向正确论文\n64\t- **标题**: \"From Reasoning to Agentic: Credit Assignment in Reinforcement Learning for Large Language Models\"\n65\t- **作者**: Chenchen Zhang（单一作者）\n66\t- **Venue/Year**: arXiv, April 2026\n67\t- **关键内容**:\n68\t  - 47 种 CA 方法（41 core + 6 adjacent enablers），2024-2026 时间范围\n69\t  - 二维分类：粒度（token, segment, step, turn, multi-agent）x 方法论（MC, TD, model-based, game-theoretic, information-theoretic）\n70\t  - 涵盖 reasoning RL 和 agentic RL 两个 regime\n71\t  - 附带 reporting checklist + benchmark protocol specification + method selection decision tree\n72\t- **与我们的关系**: 提供 credit assignment 全景图；我们的 sign misattribution 诊断属于其分类中 under-explored 的 failure mode 分析\n73\t\n74\t## 6. HiPER (2602.16165) — 实验设置确认\n75\t\n76\t- **arXiv ID**: 2602.16165 → 指向正确论文\n77\t- **标题**: \"HiPER: Hierarchical Reinforcement Learning with Explicit Credit Assignment for Large Language Model Agents\"\n78\t- **作者**: Jiangweizhi Peng, Yuanxin Liu, Ruida Zhou, Charles Fleming, Zhaoran Wang, Alfredo Garcia, Mingyi Hong\n79\t- **Venue/Year**: arXiv, February 2026\n80\t- **实验设置详细数据**:\n81\t  - 模型：Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct, Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct\n82\t  - ALFWorld: 95.3% (1.5B), 97.4% (7B)\n83\t  - GRPO baseline: 71.1% (1.5B), 85.4% (7B)\n84\t  - GiGPO baseline: 被引为 \"best prior method\"（HiPER +8.6% over GiGPO on 1.5B, +6.6% on 7B）\n85\t  - WebShop: 83.3% (7B)\n86\t  - 训练：150 epochs, 3 random seeds\n87\t  - Prompt template: Plan-Execute (HiPER) vs ReAct (baselines)\n88\t  - 训练效率：7B 约 50 steps 超过 80% success（PPO/GRPO 需 ~140 steps, 2.8x 加速）\n89\t- **与我们的关系**: 追求 SOTA performance via hierarchical architecture；我们做 mechanism diagnosis\n90\t\n91\t---\n92\t\n93\t## 总结表\n94\t\n95\t| 论文 | 验证状态 | arXiv ID | Venue | 关键修正/备注 |\n96\t|------|---------|----------|-------|--------------|\n97\t| GAGPO | PASS | 2605.13217 | arXiv 2026 | 标题 \"Generalized Advantage\"（\"Grouped Value Proxy\" 是方法术语） |\n98\t| MT-GRPO | PASS | 2505.11821 | arXiv 2025 | 不含 ALFWorld，评测在 QA 数据集 |\n99\t| iStar | PASS | 2509.19199 | ICLR 2026 | 不含 ALFWorld，评测在 WebShop/VisualSokoban/SOTOPIA |\n100\t| ArCHer | PASS | 2402.19446 | ICML 2024 | 确认 venue |\n101\t| CA Survey | PASS | 2604.09459 | arXiv 2026 | 单一作者，47 方法确认 |\n102\t| HiPER | CONFIRMED | 2602.16165 | arXiv 2026 | 97.4%(7B)/95.3%(1.5B), GRPO 71.1%/85.4% |\n103\t\n104\t## Positioning 启示\n105\t\n106\t1. **共识趋势**: 竞品一致走向 finer-grained credit (turn-level, step-level, hierarchical)\n107\t2. **我们的 contrarian**: Episode-level (coarser) 消除 sign misattribution，诊断 \"更细不一定更好\" 的反直觉结论\n108\t3. **差异化轴**: 竞品追求 performance improvement；我们做 mechanism diagnosis + contrarian solution\n109\t4. **Turn-PPO 最直接竞品**: 发现相似问题 (\"uniform advantage\" ≈ 我们的 sign misattribution subset)，但解法相反（finer vs coarser）\n110\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01M8ccfgPjsRhMzeCytoYGzb","session_id":"865e8d8a-d167-43f7-87ae-b7ba5c42080f","uuid":"f7ed4538-4e11-4a81-ba56-b3add3503ea8","timestamp":"2026-05-17T14:01:58.085Z"}
